---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Meet Our Founder — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Ajai Blue-Saunders, Certified Peer Grief Educator and founder of Glorious Health Ministries."
>
  <section class="section stack stack-loose">
    <div class="section-heading-row section-heading-row--center">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">My Story</p>
        <h1>Ajai Blue-Saunders</h1>
        <p class="kicker kicker-accent">Certified Peer Grief Educator</p>
      </div>
      <div class="motif-divider">
        <img
          src="/images/dove-hands.png"
          alt=""
          class="motif-divider-icon"
          width="289"
          height="342"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid about-content-grid">
      <div class="stack about-copy">
        <p>
          Ajai (A'jay) Blue-Saunders has been involved with program development and nonprofit
          management for over 40 years. She has a background in Grief and Loss partially gained
          through her educational experience (a bachelor's degree in philosophy &amp; religion)
          which has been further enhanced by experiencing the loss of her father, mother, older
          sister, brother, young granddaughter and finally her husband John in 2015. Currently she
          resides in the Metro Richmond, Virginia area with her adult daughter with disabilities and
          together they are learning and attempting to live a fulfilled life without him.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ajai is a Certified Grief Educator working with women to navigate the ocean of grief
          through strong Christian beliefs and faith. This support includes offering a listening,
          understanding ear, crying with someone who mourns, or praying for them in their presence.
          She formerly was a peer facilitator at a local widow's support group for over 4 years; an
          active panelist on community and national forums discussing grief, loss and healing, and
          she can be found as a presenter on the national PBS media documentary "Speaking Grief"
          which helps grievers and those supporting others in grief.
        </p>
        <p>
          Her master's degree is in Journalism which she has utilized to share her grief journey by
          writing a monthly blog (see <a href="/sisterhood/">Sisterhood section</a>) for Hope for
          Widows Foundation for many years and she enjoys sharing wisdom, resources and compassion
          to make the world a better place to live and thrive. She has served on several local and
          national nonprofit boards, including the Board of Directors for Hope for Widows Foundation
          for 2 years, helping to strengthen its impact on widows worldwide.
        </p>
        <p>
          As a trained and skilled traditional herbalist (affectionately called Dr. AJ) for over 30
          years, she marries her knowledge and experiences to facilitate workshops using God's herbs
          to heal and restore widows through the grief journey. Her workshops are encouraging and
          uplifting, while sensitive to all while she ministers ways to heal.
        </p>
        <p>
          Please contact her to arrange for a session/workshop or for general grief resources and
          support (see <a href="/connection/">Connection section</a>).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-video-col">
        <div class="video-card">
          <p class="kicker">Watch</p>
          <h2 class="video-heading">Hear From Ajai</h2>
          <div class="video-frame">
            <iframe
              title="Ajai shares how faith carried her through grief"
              src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?height=476&href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Freel%2F1396339435742929%2F&show_text=false&width=267&t=0"
              width="267"
              height="476"
              style="border:none;overflow:hidden"
              scrolling="no"
              frameborder="0"
              loading="lazy"
              allowfullscreen
              allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; web-share"
            ></iframe>
          </div>
          <p class="video-caption">
            Ajai shares, in her own words, how faith carried her through grief.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="section-divider about-section-divider" />

    <div class="stack text-center">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Let's Connect</p>
        <h2 class="about-cta-title">Ready to connect with Ajai?</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Reach out about a gathering, a speaking invitation, or one-on-one grief support.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <Button href="/contact/" type="button">Contact Ajai</Button>
        <Button href="/gatherings/" type="button" variant="outline"
          >See Upcoming Gatherings</Button
        >
      </div>

      <img
        src="/images/headshot.jpeg"
        alt="Ms. Ajai Blue-Saunders, Certified Peer Grief Educator"
        class="about-photo"
        width="1024"
        height="1024"
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
